<title>GREECE: GREEK TAXPAYERS PAID MORE TAXES IN 1996.</title>
<headline>GREEK TAXPAYERS PAID MORE TAXES IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece collected 652.4 billion drachmas from personal income and corporate taxes in 1996, up 23.2 percent on 1995, the finance ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>Declared taxable income rose to 11.306 trillion drachmas in 1996 from 9.956 trillion in 1995, an increase of 11.9 percent, it said. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
